# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — nothing here may ever be committed.
#
# The YouTube control plane reads a Google OAuth client from a path given by
# configuration and stores its tokens OUTSIDE this repository. These patterns are the
# backstop for a mistake, not the mechanism: the real rule is that credentials live in
# %LOCALAPPDATA%\BillFindsOut, never in the working tree.
#
# Patterns are deliberately narrow. A broad rule like `*secret*` or `*.json` would
# swallow legitimate source — this project keeps episode configs, storyboards, timing
# maps and asset manifests in .json, and any of them going silently untracked would be a
# far more expensive accident than it looks.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
client_secret*.json
*client_secret*.json
credentials*.json
oauth*.json
token.json
tokens.json
*.token.json
youtube-token*.json
.secrets/
*.pem
*.p12

# env files, except the committed example
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# redundant archive of qa/characters/*.png, which are tracked individually
qa/characters.zip

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.google-client-path

# Creator OS local build output
app/dist/


# ElevenLabs audio factory — raw take cache lives outside the repo (see orchestrator.mjs).
# Nothing here should ever be committed, but ignore it explicitly in case of a stray copy.
/audio-factory-cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mr.Yolk — large regenerable media.
#
# This repository has no LFS. Its biggest tracked file today is a 24 MB Short, and the whole
# working tree is about 500 MB; the Mr.Yolk long-form adds roughly a gigabyte of media on its
# own. Committing that would multiply the clone size for bytes that are all reproducible from
# artifacts which ARE committed.
#
# What stays tracked is everything needed to rebuild them and to prove what they were:
#
#   data/mryolk/stock-provenance.json   provider, creator, licence, URL and sha256 per asset
#   data/mryolk/stock-research.json     the queries, and how many candidates each reviewed
#   data/mryolk/.stock-cache/           the API responses, so a rerun need not re-search
#   data/mryolk/audio-report.json       every measurement, before and after, plus the settings
#   data/mryolk/stt/                    the transcript and timings the whole edit hangs off
#   public/mryolk/assets/               the 216 extracted drawings (6.7 MB — small, permanent)
#   public/mryolk/sfx/                  the synthesised sound palette (0.9 MB, deterministic)
#
# Regenerate with, in order:
#   npm run mryolk:audio      (needs the source takes in C:\Users\ducnq\Downloads\Src)
#   npm run mryolk:stock      (needs PEXELS_API_KEY / PIXABAY_API_KEY)
#   npm run mryolk:render
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
public/mryolk/stock/
public/mryolk/audio/*.wav
out/mryolk-*.mp4
qa/mryolk/frames/
qa/mryolk/smoke/
qa/mryolk/fix/
